# Gate-authority policy (process.md §4; process-options.md "Gate authority
# levels"). One value on the last line — who ratifies a gate advance. Gates are
# DERIVED: docs/gate is computed from the artifact states by derive_gate.py, and a
# gate advances when a batch of artifacts is RATIFIED in a reviewed commit
# (Status Draft->Planned, or an SN moved out of a draft section). This level
# governs WHO may make that ratifying commit:
#   attended      — a human ratifies each batch (the default; standard §4).
#   single-ratify — LLM-gate review through G1+G2; the human ratifies the
#                   queued batch once at the phase's [g2] close; autonomous after.
#   autonomous    — every gate except G-Final closes on an independent
#                   fresh-context LLM reviewer's recorded verdict.
# A non-default level is amended into the repo by the deviation register
# (docs/gate-policy.md — scaffolded by `bootstrap.py --gate-policy`); the §4
# fixed points hold at every level. This policy value is itself hand-set — change
# it in a reviewed commit (docs/gate itself is generated, never hand-edited).
single-ratify
